  "proof_chain": [
    "The actual cylindrical range geometry forces the same Y to take physical endpoints to 0 and 1, via its genuine inverse and positive derivative; no new map is chosen.",
    "The pinned mean-value theorem on the physical closed interval gives Y(r)*(1-Y(r)) <= M*min(r-l,u-r), using the same actual derivative upper bound.",
    "The physical profile estimate k*min(r-l,u-r) <= wprime(r)/r and actual height H(r)>=h imply c >= (h^2*k/M^2)*xi*(1-xi) at the true inverse image.",
    "The actual V coefficient formula is used without changing Y/H, reference gauges, piece enumeration, cell, or state family.",
    "The optional full ReferencePrincipal criterion uses a single physical cost M_i^2 <= B*E0(sample(cell_i))^B*(h_i^2*k_i) and combines the already reviewed qualitative first clause. The global cost has its exact actual cell and sample."
  ],
  "unproved_inputs": [
    "A positive physical-profile endpoint constant k_i on each whole positive interval is an explicit input, not derived from Through03 or from mere strict positivity of wprime.",
    "The height lower and derivative upper bounds must hold for the same actual interpolated H_i and Y_i; a different comparison map is insufficient.",
    "The single B controlling the physical cost across every component is an explicit remaining material estimate. No compactness argument is asserted to make it uniform.",
    "No assumption that unscaled E0 is at least one is used. The stated physical cost itself forces its denominator positive.",
    "The physical linear lower input must also be checked on any ambient-adjacent positive component; ambient flatness does not supply it."
  ],
